{
  "transcriptVersion": 1,
  "id": "restore-happy",
  "description": "A new device of a person who was signed in, with the restore key its platform backup carried (I-49, WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §12.11.8). Discovery names restore. The device posts the restore grant as a form: grant_type urn:polaris-key:grant-type:restore, client_id, restore_id, restore_secret, its device_key and agree_key, and the pkey-proof/1 restore proof (value <restore_id>.<device_key>, the sixth line the SHA-256 of the secret). The person has already consented to this app, so the answer is a device token and the SDK holds it: no click. The key is used up. The device then enrols a key of its own, POST restore {} answering 201 {restoreId, secret}, which the client writes into the backup; a check with that id answers 200 current; and past 90 days the same call answers 201 with a new key that replaces it.",
